\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Starting models for a matched carbon-coupling comparison. Adjacent CO and bonded OCCO are placed at a Cu-side interface or Cu terrace with identical elemental loading of two C and two O atoms. The structures use the actual input coordinates; reported C--C separations are initial values. Comparing their verified relaxed structures and spectra would separate changes associated with C--C bonding from those associated with interface location.\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:coupling}{{5}{14}{Starting models for a matched carbon-coupling comparison. Adjacent CO and bonded OCCO are placed at a Cu-side interface or Cu terrace with identical elemental loading of two C and two O atoms. The structures use the actual input coordinates; reported C--C separations are initial values. Comparing their verified relaxed structures and spectra would separate changes associated with C--C bonding from those associated with interface location.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
